# Performance

- Establish an entity count and measurable budget before optimization work.
- Do not create per-soldier AI, physics bodies, pathfinders, React components, event emitters, or class graphs.
- Use formation authority, dense IDs, typed arrays, spatial indices, culling, LOD, and bounded update sets.
- Avoid allocation in hot loops; measure before adding pools.
- Keep authoritative simulation off the main thread when resolution may exceed the frame budget.
- Prefer transferable buffers before SharedArrayBuffer.
- Phaser `SpriteGPULayer` is for one-texture, very large populations with infrequent/batched buffer changes; do not rewrite it blindly every frame.
- Visual density must not change authoritative results.
- Record before/after benchmark data, hardware, browser, viewport, counts, and quality settings.
- Do not claim a performance win without measurements.
